      "task_id": "BRICK-KB-003",
      "title": "Discover documentation source files",
      "description": "**Core Objective**\nExtend discovery and ignore rules to support Markdown, reStructuredText, and plain text files while preserving relative paths, encoding, content fingerprints, and line numbers. Exclude secrets, binaries, generated output, and dependency folders.\n\n**Target Files & Roles**\n- **src/brickforge/ingestion/discovery.py**: Modify to include Markdown, reStructuredText, and plain text files in the discovery process.\n- **src/brickforge/ingestion/ignore_rules.py**: Update to include additional ignore patterns for binaries, generated files, and dependency folders.\n- **tests/unit/test_document_discovery.py**: Create to test the functionality of the document discovery and ignore rules.\n\n**Critical Technical Invariants**\n- **Imports**: Ensure `os`, `fnmatch`, `re`, and `datetime` are imported where necessary.\n- **Signatures**: Maintain the signature of `walk_registered_roots(roots, ignore_rules=None)`.\n- **Ignore Patterns**: Add patterns for `.md`, `.rst`, `.txt`, and binary file extensions to `DEFAULT_IGNORE_PATTERNS`.\n- **Mock Setups**: Use `unittest.mock` for any necessary mocking in tests.\n- **Environment Rules**: Tests should run in a clean environment with no external dependencies affecting the test outcomes.\n\n**Verification Pass Criteria**\n- The `test_document_discovery` function in `tests/unit/test_document_discovery.py` must pass without any assertion errors.\n- The verification command `python -m pytest -q tests/unit/test_document_discovery.py` must execute successfully with no test failures.",
