      "description": "### Core Objective\n- Abstract the Ollama and OpenAI chat providers behind a unified interface.\n- Ensure the interface supports `/api/chat` for Ollama and `/v1/chat/completions` for OpenAI, including streaming, model discovery, cancellation, timeouts, and normalized errors.\n\n### Target Files & Roles\n- **`src/brickforge/web/providers.py`**: Define the abstract base class for chat providers and concrete implementations for Ollama and OpenAI.\n- **`src/brickforge/web/chat.py`**: Integrate the provider interface into the existing chat engine, ensuring compatibility and functionality.\n- **`tests/unit/test_chat_providers.py`**: Write unit tests to verify the functionality and compliance of the chat providers.\n\n### Critical Technical Invariants\n- **Imports**: Ensure all necessary imports are included, such as `httpx` for HTTP requests and `typing` for type annotations.\n- **Type Signatures**: Define clear type signatures for all methods in the provider interface and implementations.\n- **Mock Setups**: Use `unittest.mock` to simulate HTTP responses for testing purposes.\n- **Environment Rules**: Tests should run locally without external dependencies, using mock data.\n\n### Verification Pass Criteria\n- The verification command `python -m pytest -q tests/unit/test_chat_providers.py` must pass without any errors or failures.\n- All tests in `tests/unit/test_chat_providers.py` must cover the functionality of streaming, model discovery, cancellation, timeouts, and error normalization for both Ollama and OpenAI providers.",
